  "security_implications": "This chunk drives message data into SHA‑3, manages key delivery (key_data, key_len, key_valid), handles entropy, and propagates escalation/error signals. The incomplete drive of msg_data_masked[0] (U1) is a critical bug that corrupts all but bit 0 of message data, leading to broken hashing and possible leakage of plaintext or key material. The unconnected integrity error (U2) allows silent data corruption in the message FIFO, bypassing fault detection and potentially enabling fault‑injection attacks. The tied‑off read path and ignored address (U3) remove a layer of access monitoring. The unused entropy precondition (A2) and lifecycle assumption (A4) are essential for maintaining side‑channel resistance and secure state separation.",
